Alembic migrations
==================

The migration environment reads the database URL from `DATABASE_URL`.
When it is not set, it connects to the PostgreSQL service from
`docker-compose.yml` at:

    postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:postgres@localhost:40321/postgres

Create an autogenerated migration:

    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "create initial tables"

Create an empty migration:

    uv run alembic revision -m "migration description"

Apply migrations:

    uv run alembic upgrade head

Revision IDs and filenames are assigned globally and sequentially:
`0001_description.py`, `0002_description.py`, and so on. Do not pass
`--rev-id` manually and do not use non-numeric revision IDs.
